00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:06.869 align:start position:0%
how does the voting system in the  council of the european union work  the council is made up of member state  representatives  who meet regularly to adopt and discuss  eu legislation  decisions at council meetings are taken  by vote  the council can only vote if a majority  of its members is present  15 out of 28.  there are three types of voting  procedure simple majority  qualified majority and unanimity  simple majority voting is used for  procedural issues  such as the rules governing council  committees  it requires the majority of member  states 15 out of a total of 28  to vote in favor of the proposal  qualified majority is used for the 80 of  eu legislation  adopted through the ordinary legislative  procedure also known as co-decision  a qualified majority is reached if two  conditions are met  55 percent of member states vote in  favor in practice this means  16 out of 28. the proposal is supported  by member states representing at least  65  of the total eu population this is the  double majority rule  proposals can be blocked by a group of  at least four member states  representing more than 35 percent of the  eu population  this is called a blocking minority  not that complicated but wait there's a  catch  this qualified majority rule is in use  from november 2014  but until 2017 member states can still  request to use the previous rule  under this rule each member state has a  certain number of votes  based on their population size reaching  a qualified majority  needs votes out of a total of 352  from at least 15 member states  now for unanimity i guess it's pretty  self-explanatory  it requires everyone to agree or abstain  if a council member abstains the other  ministers can still reach unanimity  unanimity voting is used for some  specific areas  mentioned in the eu treaties such as  citizenship  eu membership and taxation  after the council votes on legislative  texts the results are immediately made  available to the public  now you know how voting in the council  of the eu works  find out more on the website at  concillium.europa.eu  you
 

